00:26:49,975 --> 00:26:52,145
Yesterday you had it
on the truck bed.

500
00:26:52,178 --> 00:26:55,515
- Oh, yeah.
We've met before, haven't we?

501
00:26:55,548 --> 00:26:58,050
Why, you my fair lady,
you're Guinevere.

502
00:26:58,083 --> 00:27:00,553
But I don't seem to
recall your name, sir.

503
00:27:00,587 --> 00:27:03,088
- Aw, cut the baloney out, huh?
You want a ride?

504
00:27:03,122 --> 00:27:06,158
- My other name is Michele,
he's Buz.

505
00:27:06,192 --> 00:27:07,393
- Michele and Buz.

506
00:27:07,427 --> 00:27:08,995
- I'll allow it.
- Mine's Critter.

507
00:27:09,028 --> 00:27:09,995
- Critter?

508
00:27:10,028 --> 00:27:11,097
- Yeah, you know,
like a cowboy's horse

509
00:27:11,130 --> 00:27:13,032
or a wayward cat
without a home.

510
00:27:13,065 --> 00:27:14,833
- Look, come on.
You want a ride?

511
00:27:14,867 --> 00:27:16,168
- Yes, we do.

512
00:27:16,202 --> 00:27:17,270
- Whatta ya mean, we?

513
00:27:17,303 --> 00:27:18,705
- Well, Traveler and I.

514
00:27:18,738 --> 00:27:20,307
- Aw, now look, wise guy,

515
00:27:20,340 --> 00:27:21,875
I ain't carrying no
beat up old motorcycle

516
00:27:21,908 --> 00:27:23,108
on the back of my car.

517
00:27:23,142 --> 00:27:25,045
- Well, you won't have to,
I got a tow bar.

518
00:27:25,078 --> 00:27:26,412
- Oh, well, you got to have
an upper hitch

519
00:27:26,445 --> 00:27:27,480
for one of them to work.

520
00:27:27,513 --> 00:27:29,448
- Ah, it just so happens
I have one of those too.

521
00:27:31,050 --> 00:27:32,452
- You know, in fact,
I have a car too,

522
00:27:32,485 --> 00:27:34,787
so I guess
I don't need a ride.

523
00:27:36,588 --> 00:27:39,192
- Three hours
and four bumpers later.

524
00:27:40,660 --> 00:27:42,995
- We'll take the sidewalk
for another couple of miles.

525
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:49,135
- Now, they picked up Joan Baez.

526
00:27:51,938 --> 00:27:55,475
- Is there a papoose
tied to the motorcycle.

527
00:27:55,508 --> 00:27:57,943
- You know, I can't
get over your name.

528
00:27:57,977 --> 00:27:59,778
It's a funny name, Critter.

529
00:27:59,812 --> 00:28:01,848
- Fellas gave me that name
when I was in preschool.

530
00:28:01,882 --> 00:28:02,848
- I'm back!

531
00:28:02,882 --> 00:28:04,517
[ALL COMMENTATORS LAUGHING]

532
00:28:04,550 --> 00:28:07,753
- I helped the native...
[indistinct]

533
00:28:07,787 --> 00:28:09,588
- Yeah? You're kidding.

534
00:28:09,622 --> 00:28:11,490
- Anybody notice
that I'm here now?

535
00:28:11,523 --> 00:28:14,527
- ...I'll bet you got
a college education.

536
00:28:14,560 --> 00:28:17,763
- Well, yes and no.
I didn't get a degree

537
00:28:17,797 --> 00:28:21,200
but I tried my hand at
Columbia and Berkeley.

538
00:28:21,233 --> 00:28:22,635
- Wish I could've gone
to one of them.

539
00:28:22,668 --> 00:28:24,137
- Come on,
I just teleported here.

540
00:28:24,170 --> 00:28:25,538
It's impressive!

541
00:28:25,572 --> 00:28:27,773
- Look, I hate to butt in on
this real brilliant conversation

542
00:28:27,807 --> 00:28:29,708
but we gotta
bing it outta here.

543
00:28:29,742 --> 00:28:31,710
Waitress?
Check please.

544
00:28:31,743 --> 00:28:33,245
Now how about it,
Critter, old pal?

545
00:28:33,278 --> 00:28:34,847
It seems to me this place
oughta have change

546
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:37,550
for a 50,
maybe even a 100, huh?

547
00:28:39,185 --> 00:28:42,322
- Three waters, those little
fish shaped soup crackers...

548
00:28:44,857 --> 00:28:46,425
- I'm an icky elf.

549
00:28:49,862 --> 00:28:51,063
- Ever since I got back,

550
00:28:51,097 --> 00:28:53,198
I've been carrying my billfold
full of Nepalese money.

551
00:28:53,232 --> 00:28:54,900
- From the land of nipple.

552
00:28:54,933 --> 00:28:58,003
- But you can try to get it
cashed if you like.

553
00:28:58,037 --> 00:29:00,773
- You tell funny
foreign currency jokes.

554
00:29:03,677 --> 00:29:05,878
- I'm Critter. Eh?

555
00:29:05,912 --> 00:29:07,447
- Okay baby,
show all yours.

556
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:08,482
- Here?

557
00:29:12,552 --> 00:29:14,587
- Your money's from Senegal.

558
00:29:14,620 --> 00:29:16,755
- 10 bucks?
That's all you've got?

559
00:29:16,788 --> 00:29:18,658
- I had to buy...
[indistinct]

560
00:29:18,692 --> 00:29:20,227
- But you were back
at a cash register.

561
00:29:20,260 --> 00:29:21,862
- And took what was
coming to me.

562
00:29:21,895 --> 00:29:24,430
It amounted to 14 dollars.

563
00:29:24,463 --> 00:29:26,132
- Well, that's just great.

564
00:29:26,165 --> 00:29:28,167
- You didn't have to
take out FICA.

565
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:29,768
- With this tab coming to 4.50,

566
00:29:29,802 --> 00:29:32,605
that'll leave us a lousy 5.50
to get to L.A.

567
00:29:32,638 --> 00:29:35,408
- Look, I didn't take any more
from the cash register

568
00:29:35,442 --> 00:29:37,543
than 14 dollars.

569
00:29:37,577 --> 00:29:38,878
That was mine.

570
00:29:38,912 --> 00:29:40,880
- That was my yearly salary.

571
00:29:41,915 --> 00:29:44,550
- Okay boy, can you take care
of your own share?

572
00:29:44,583 --> 00:29:46,685
- Yeah.
- Natural born cheapskates.

573
00:29:46,718 --> 00:29:48,588
- I can come up
with my own share.

574
00:29:49,722 --> 00:29:51,623
- Uh, here's some
Guatemalan quetzal.

575
00:29:51,657 --> 00:29:53,960
- And 15 dollars more to boot.

576
00:29:55,328 --> 00:29:59,365
- Why, we oughta be able to
reach Los Angeles with 20 bucks.

577
00:29:59,398 --> 00:30:01,233
- Come on.

578
00:30:01,267 --> 00:30:02,602
- Let's get some of those
pillowy little mints

579
00:30:02,635 --> 00:30:04,437
at the cash register.

580
00:30:08,942 --> 00:30:12,112
- Well, I should get a little
to go box and my butter pat.

581
00:30:15,415 --> 00:30:17,950
- He yanked the engine
off a KitchenAid blender.

582
00:30:22,022 --> 00:30:23,055
[CROW SCREAMS]

583
00:30:23,088 --> 00:30:25,958
He's throwing us violently
into the next scene.

584
00:30:27,560 --> 00:30:29,362
- Hi, can I be in your movie?

585
00:30:34,067 --> 00:30:36,802
- This makes me want to throw
hard candy at people.

586
00:30:38,070 --> 00:30:41,207
- So, they blew the 15 bucks
on a dune buggy rental.

587
00:30:46,045 --> 00:30:48,013
- We're thinking of adopting.

588
00:30:52,218 --> 00:30:54,853
- A new motorized
beach bathtub.

589
00:30:57,357 --> 00:30:59,592
- And the movie ends.
No.

590
00:31:01,893 --> 00:31:04,230
- Let's drive through
the oil soaked ducks again.

591
00:31:04,263 --> 00:31:06,332
[SCREAMING]

592
00:31:08,768 --> 00:31:12,272
- Well, apparently the story
is none of our business.

593
00:31:12,305 --> 00:31:13,572
- What a ride!

594
00:31:13,605 --> 00:31:14,607
- Enjoyed it?

595
00:31:14,640 --> 00:31:16,175
Hey, you wanna go for a ride?

596
00:31:16,208 --> 00:31:17,810
- Uh, no.
I guess I'll pass for now.

597
00:31:17,843 --> 00:31:19,378
Thanks a lot.
- Alright.

598
00:31:19,412 --> 00:31:20,913
- Well, I don't know
about you guys, but...

599
00:31:20,947 --> 00:31:21,913
- I'm an icky elf.

600
00:31:21,947 --> 00:31:23,315
- ...I'm thirsty.

601
00:31:23,348 --> 00:31:24,717
- So long, odd acquaintance,

602
00:31:24,750 --> 00:31:27,420
who inexplicably gave us
rides in your dune buggy.

603
00:31:29,722 --> 00:31:31,923
- There goes...
- You can say that a...

604
00:31:31,957 --> 00:31:32,958
- One o...

605
00:31:34,293 --> 00:31:36,095
- You and Buz planned
to get married in L.A.?

606
00:31:36,128 --> 00:31:38,998
- You don't need to
spell in front of me.

607
00:31:39,032 --> 00:31:42,102
- I'm riding with him to L.A.

608
00:31:42,135 --> 00:31:44,237
He's going to help me
get started as a dancer.

609
00:31:44,270 --> 00:31:45,838
His sister can help me.

610
00:31:45,872 --> 00:31:47,940
That's all there is to it.

611
00:31:47,973 --> 00:31:50,743
- Well, my naive country girl,
I hope it's that simple.

612
00:31:50,777 --> 00:31:52,412
- Uh-huh.
I'm gonna be a dancer.

613
00:31:52,445 --> 00:31:54,713
- Maybe Buz does seem
a little crude at times,

614
00:31:54,747 --> 00:31:56,315
but you just have to
get to know him.

615
00:31:56,348 --> 00:31:58,017
- It helps if you meet
the other elf.

616
00:31:58,050 --> 00:31:59,085
- Like two days?

617
00:32:00,987 --> 00:32:02,022
Hey...

618
00:32:02,055 --> 00:32:03,155
- My name's Critter.

619
00:32:03,188 --> 00:32:04,690
- ...don't pay any attention
to me.

620
00:32:04,723 --> 00:32:06,225
What you do
is your own business

621
00:32:06,258 --> 00:32:08,093
and it's really
no concern of mine.

622
00:32:08,127 --> 00:32:11,863
- That's right,
it is no concern of yours.

623
00:32:11,897 --> 00:32:15,402
I'm going to become a dancer,
Critter, and a good one.

624
00:32:15,435 --> 00:32:17,803
You said yourself I'm pretty.

625
00:32:17,837 --> 00:32:20,473
I'm good at dancing too.

626
00:32:20,507 --> 00:32:22,008
- Compared to Stephen Hawking.

627
00:32:22,042 --> 00:32:24,110
- ...when you're wet
and angry... [indistinct]

628
00:32:24,143 --> 00:32:28,247
- Critter, stop teasing me.
I want you to take me seriously.

629
00:32:28,280 --> 00:32:30,248
- Okay, little numby head.

630
00:32:30,282 --> 00:32:32,252
- I'm taking you seriously.

631
00:32:33,652 --> 00:32:36,288
- Thank you. Anyway,
the thing about dancing

632
00:32:36,322 --> 00:32:38,190
is when you dance...

633
00:32:38,223 --> 00:32:40,527
[MUFFLED SOUNDS]

634
00:32:41,527 --> 00:32:43,662
- Hey, he's mine,
take your hands off him!

635
00:32:43,695 --> 00:32:47,867
- Get lost.

636
00:32:47,900 --> 00:32:49,602
[SHOUTS]
- Stop it, please!

637
00:32:49,635 --> 00:32:51,237
- I'm having Critter's varmint.

638
00:32:51,270 --> 00:32:55,173
- Listen you, you stay away
from Michele, understand?

639
00:32:55,207 --> 00:32:56,875
- Why don't you
let her decide that?

640
00:32:58,610 --> 00:33:00,647
- Yeah.

641
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:02,648
Why not?

642
00:33:02,682 --> 00:33:05,150
- Are you only here
in California to... [indistinct]

643
00:33:05,183 --> 00:33:06,818
broken down old motorcycle

644
00:33:06,852 --> 00:33:09,188
or are you here
for a reason?

645
00:33:09,222 --> 00:33:10,523
Now you tell him.

646
00:33:12,625 --> 00:33:15,795
[SHOUTS]
- I'm allergic to shellfish.

647
00:33:15,828 --> 00:33:17,263
- I'm here to be a dancer!

648
00:33:17,297 --> 00:33:19,798
- Going to go
into voice work too.

649
00:33:22,033 --> 00:33:24,437
- Well, now the whole picnic
is ruined.

650
00:33:27,173 --> 00:33:29,075
- I'm a crumby Critter.

651
00:33:29,108 --> 00:33:32,112
[♪♪♪]

652
00:33:36,015 --> 00:33:38,017
- We're in Alberta,
it looks like.

653
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:42,888
- Find your number?

654
00:33:42,922 --> 00:33:45,157
- Uh, yeah.

655
00:33:45,190 --> 00:33:46,758
- Will this be cash or charge?

656
00:33:46,792 --> 00:33:48,627
- Uh, will you take
a toothpick?

657
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:49,660
- Cash.

658
00:33:50,797 --> 00:33:53,665
- On second thought,
I'll just put it on my gun.

659
00:33:55,735 --> 00:33:58,370
- Hey, that guy's totally
pistol whipped, man.

660
00:34:02,208 --> 00:34:03,743
- Oh, he flicked a booger.

661
00:34:07,247 --> 00:34:10,650
- Oh shoot,
it's all green stamps.

662
00:34:13,152 --> 00:34:14,320
- Sounds like Max and 99

663
00:34:14,353 --> 00:34:16,455
should be sneaking
around outside.

664
00:34:21,893 --> 00:34:25,465
- Don't forget your
Roman Gabriel collector's plate.

665
00:34:28,367 --> 00:34:30,770
- Oh shoot,
they're closed-- oh.

666
00:34:34,973 --> 00:34:37,377
- I locked the car keys
in the store.

667
00:34:39,945 --> 00:34:41,680
- Did you get
my Marathon Bar?

668
00:34:41,713 --> 00:34:42,748
- Hey, what the devil's
going on?

669
00:34:42,782 --> 00:34:44,783
- Stay in the car.
Get behind the wheel.

670
00:34:45,852 --> 00:34:47,753
- Get more behind the wheel,
come on.

671
00:34:47,787 --> 00:34:49,155
- Where's the attendant?

672
00:34:49,188 --> 00:34:50,590
- Sound asleep.

673
00:34:50,623 --> 00:34:52,225
Okay, roll this baby
out of here.

674
00:34:52,258 --> 00:34:53,725
- Buz, what have you done?

675
00:34:53,758 --> 00:34:55,260
Have you gone crazy?

676
00:34:55,293 --> 00:34:56,662
- Move it!
- I've got 50 bucks.

677
00:34:56,695 --> 00:34:59,098
We've got dune buggy rides
all week.

678
00:35:02,435 --> 00:35:04,270
- Hey, crimes like this
never happen anymore

679
00:35:04,303 --> 00:35:06,505
now that we have McGruff.

680
00:35:11,743 --> 00:35:14,080
- I hope we're here
in time for folk rock.

681
00:35:15,213 --> 00:35:17,183
- Hey, they drove straight
to Christmas Village

682
00:35:17,217 --> 00:35:19,285
to blow the wad.

683
00:35:19,318 --> 00:35:23,522
[CHRISTMAS MUSIC]

684
00:35:24,890 --> 00:35:27,593
♪ Oh it's lovely weather
For a surfboard ♪

685
00:35:27,627 --> 00:35:29,895
♪ Together with you ♪

686
00:35:32,097 --> 00:35:35,735
♪ Where the Bank of America
Whoa ho ♪

687
00:35:35,768 --> 00:35:38,770
[♪♪♪]

688
00:35:41,573 --> 00:35:43,275
- A bunny from heaven.

689
00:35:48,213 --> 00:35:50,115
- Hey pally, huh!

690
00:35:54,953 --> 00:35:55,922
- Dr. Doolittle?

691
00:35:55,955 --> 00:35:57,022
That doesn't look like
Eddie Murphy.

692
00:35:57,055 --> 00:35:58,057
- No.

693
00:36:01,493 --> 00:36:04,530
- I think someone slipped us
their vacation videos.

694
00:36:08,133 --> 00:36:09,102
- Okay, keep it coming.

695
00:36:09,135 --> 00:36:11,970
I'm not convinced
that they're in L.A. yet.

696
00:36:13,038 --> 00:36:17,142
- An 18-story office building?
This could only be L.A.

697
00:36:18,945 --> 00:36:22,047
♪ Oh Charles Manson
Walks the streets ♪

698
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:24,950
♪ The Zodiac killer's at large ♪

699
00:36:24,983 --> 00:36:27,920
♪ Charles Bukowski
Is puking out the window ♪

700
00:36:27,953 --> 00:36:30,555
♪ And Santa Claus
Is on his way ♪

701
00:36:30,588 --> 00:36:31,590
- Hey!

702
00:36:34,860 --> 00:36:38,397
- Merry Christmas everyone,
let's go to the haunted house.

703
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:43,702
- Boo, sir.

704
00:36:49,842 --> 00:36:51,210
- Thanks for the car, buddy.

705
00:36:52,243 --> 00:36:55,213
- Yup, I know
the werewolf here.

706
00:36:57,950 --> 00:36:58,917
[BLUES MUSIC]

707
00:36:58,950 --> 00:37:01,720
- Wow, this is like
"Eat," times four.

708
00:37:03,955 --> 00:37:05,390
- Love this.

709
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:10,295
- Yeah, see how they
shake their boobs.

710
00:37:17,770 --> 00:37:18,870
- Man, think of the lucky kid

711
00:37:18,903 --> 00:37:20,673
who stumbles on
this haunted house.

712
00:37:20,707 --> 00:37:21,707
- Yeah-hah.

713
00:37:22,708 --> 00:37:24,843
Look, something.

714
00:37:30,482 --> 00:37:33,052
- Stacy Keach.

715
00:37:34,320 --> 00:37:35,553
- Table for three.

716
00:37:35,587 --> 00:37:37,757
- Uh, butts or breasts?

717
00:37:37,790 --> 00:37:39,092
- Would you like to sit down?

718
00:37:39,125 --> 00:37:40,425
- Get lost.

719
00:37:40,458 --> 00:37:41,927
- I've worked here
six year, sir.

720
00:37:41,960 --> 00:37:44,630
It's gonna be hard to find
a place I don't know about.

721
00:37:52,003 --> 00:37:54,007
- Is that my friend,
Count Chocula?

722
00:37:54,040 --> 00:37:56,342
- You enjoying the show, pal?

723
00:37:56,375 --> 00:37:57,943
- Yeah.

724
00:38:00,045 --> 00:38:01,080
- You guys are broke,

725
00:38:01,113 --> 00:38:03,015
go home and watch
the late night movie on TV.

726
00:38:03,048 --> 00:38:05,283
- Do you know if
Van Ryan's Express is on?

727
00:38:06,318 --> 00:38:08,087
- Now don't get cute, son.

728
00:38:10,222 --> 00:38:12,358
- Or my doppelganger
will kick you out.

729
00:38:15,260 --> 00:38:17,062
- The Mt. Rushmore of ugly.

730
00:38:17,095 --> 00:38:20,165
- We're just waiting for
the show to get over with.

731
00:38:20,198 --> 00:38:22,468
That's my sister up there.

732
00:38:22,502 --> 00:38:23,635
The one in the middle?

733
00:38:23,668 --> 00:38:25,470
- The one who just
fell off the stage?

734
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:30,342
- D-- Donna?
Where are you going?

735
00:38:36,948 --> 00:38:38,583
- Bye Cindy, good luck!

736
00:38:38,617 --> 00:38:41,320
[APPLAUSE]

737
00:38:45,190 --> 00:38:46,525
- Thank you,
I'm the one who jumped.

738
00:38:46,558 --> 00:38:48,093
Thank you.

739
00:38:51,830 --> 00:38:52,798
- This show made possible

740
00:38:52,832 --> 00:38:55,433
by a grant from
the Onan Foundation.

741
00:38:55,467 --> 00:38:58,603
- Hey, I forgot to tell you
about our pasta special.

742
00:38:58,637 --> 00:39:00,205
- Follow me.

743
00:39:04,477 --> 00:39:07,245
- What?
Ah ah ah... choo.

744
00:39:07,278 --> 00:39:09,548
Ah ah ah...

745
00:39:09,582 --> 00:39:11,117
[♪♪♪]

746
00:39:11,150 --> 00:39:12,952
♪ You and I... ♪

747
00:39:12,985 --> 00:39:14,087
- Now they're singing

748
00:39:14,120 --> 00:39:16,822
"Keep Your Brown Chukka
